
You are an AI coding agent working in this repository.

CRITICAL: Always read and follow these files first:
1) AGENTS.md (working rules and repo contract)
2) SPEC.md (phased implementation plan + checkpoints)
3) CLAUDE.md (architecture notes, build commands, conventions)

PHASE DISCIPLINE
- Work on exactly ONE phase at a time as defined in SPEC.md.
- Do not implement features from later phases.
- At the end of work, ensure the current phase checkpoint is satisfied (or clearly state what is missing and why).

ENGINEERING RULES
- Keep changes small and incremental; prefer minimal diffs.
- Keep the project building at all times. If build breaks, fix it immediately before proceeding.
- **Before building**: Always kill the running Muesli app first (`killall Muesli` or quit from menu bar) to avoid build failures from locked executable.
- **After making code changes**: Always rebuild and relaunch the app automatically. Never prompt the user to rebuild or relaunch—just do it.
- Prefer Swift 6 concurrency (async/await) and @Observable for state.
- Follow the repo's SwiftUI style: minimal, clean, no clutter.
- Avoid adding new dependencies unless SPEC.md explicitly requires it.

CODE ORGANIZATION
- One primary type per file.
- Put reusable UI components under Views/Components.
- Services are pure-ish and orchestrated by the ViewModel; do not scatter state across views.

SAFETY / DATA
- Do not introduce telemetry or cloud upload.
- Do not write secrets/keys into the repo.
- Avoid committing large binaries (models, audio, build artifacts).

WHEN EDITING
- If a change impacts architecture, output format, permissions, or phase scope:
  - update SPEC.md accordingly (briefly)
  - explain the rationale in your response

DOCUMENTATION UPDATES (after completing work)
- After debugging, stabbing, or completing a phase, evaluate if core docs need updates:
  - Review AGENTS.md "Documentation Updates" section for guidance
  - Update AGENTS.md for technical constraints, build procedures, architecture changes
  - Update CLAUDE.md for detailed pitfalls, code patterns, testing strategies
  - Update SPEC.md for phase adjustments, checkpoint refinements, architecture decisions
  - Update .cursorrules for agent workflow improvements
- Focus on learnings that help future work: recurring patterns, architectural decisions, constraints, procedures that differ from expectations
- Be selective and concise; maintain consistency with existing documentation style

OUTPUT REQUIREMENTS (every response after code changes)
- What changed (brief)
- Files modified (list, including documentation if updated)
- How to build/test (commands)
- Phase checkpoint status (met / not met, and what remains)